WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Agent Readiness Gate — production evidence for an AI agent, inside your own cloud, in two weeks.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:16.000
The problem: agents complete 66% of real tasks (humans 72%), yet only 5% of companies have every critical control, and the average organisation logs 54 agent incidents a year.

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:31.000
What the Gate checks: an agent-specific attack pack mapped to OWASP ASI01–ASI10; an evaluation harness seeded from your real failures; a cost-per-task baseline; a permission audit; an Agent Bill of Materials; the eight-area readiness scorecard.

4
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:44.000
The deliverable: one Evidence Report written for engineering, the CISO and audit — produced inside your estate, with pass rates, mapped findings, cost per task and the BOM.

5
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:54.000
How the sprint runs: days 1–2 scope and access; days 3–7 the thin slice and the attack pack; days 8–9 the Evidence Report; day 10 a sixty-minute readout.

6
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Published prices: $7,500 for the sprint on one agent; $25,000 for the Full Gate on a tool-using agent; $45,000 for a multi-agent or MCP-connected estate.

7
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Tell us the use case; we'll tell you where it would stall. Book a 30-minute call at rainkernel.com or write to hello@rainkernel.com.
